  "coverage": [
    "Exact source dataflow recognizes an ordinary one-row Matrix comprehension producing F64, solely consumed by SumColumns and then literal scalar selector1. Sole-consumer identity aliases require identical schemas and one definition. The bounded straight original finish/continuation path may include only proved copies, no-ops and those exact calls. Escaped intermediates, integers, another axis/selector, rectangles and incompatible grouping retain their existing path.",
    "The emitted fold reuses the existing Cranelift numeric-map scalar DAG, branches/phi words, current immutable matrix pins and checked range cursors. It starts at positive zero and adds each source result in original iteration order, without reassociation or FMA. Its actual output bank is empty while logical source/output counts and bounds remain admitted.",
    "Entry checks exact selected factories and original producer, sum and selector shapes. Conservative bounds retain logical intermediate output bytes/elements, including the singleton sum for an empty producer, finite comparison/compute/cloned/temporary/node limits, physical coexistence and complete original-CFG replay credit. Failed scalar arithmetic or bounds discards the private attempt and replays the original source error. Some finite caps keep the ordinary route.",
    "A completed map drops all source/matrix pins and parks only its primitive fold and immutable coordinates with tracked metadata/node/work reservations. Only the exact original exit-to-finish visits may follow, at the checked epoch and same budget account. Completion removes the empty builder, performs normal original continuation admission/retirement and writes the selected scalar into its original native local. The shared post-action join retains original downstream control and scalar output publication.",
    "Six new tests cover original/decoded artifacts, real Object emission/table-image reconstruction and restored descriptors, empty input and exact F64 order/bits, nonterminal scalar use, nested conditional/range comprehensions, partial bounds/unsigned-division source errors, all nine finite dimensions, distinct atomic old outputs, aliases, mutation/interleaving refusal, metadata forgery, cleanup/retry and ordinary unsupported routes. Existing actual Cholesky and Gram-Schmidt tests require real fold selection and zero sum/select library calls. Both exact Huffman work equations remain unchanged under policy139. No benchmark source was rewritten."
  ],
